Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 11:40:43 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07645/11362] [outer-loop] grid-fallback live-discovery A/B on
 bp35: honest NULL vs the real metric

Generalization-Testing-Floor validation of the bp35 perception fix
(GAP-ARC-BP35-CLICK-CANDIDATE-GENERATION-MISS) against LIVE DISCOVERY
instead of candidate coverage. Real E3AgentPolicy frame-only, adapter
disabled, proposer=None, budget=400, seed=20260719 (matches the
arc_live_oracle_gap baseline), flag OFF vs ON, paired.

Result: OFF levels=0 reached=L0 393 actions; ON levels=0 reached=L0
393 actions. Zero discovery delta -- the coverage fix (21->15 misses)
does NOT move the deliverable metric. And the ON arm is 37% slower
(2251s vs 1642s) from the up-to-64-candidates/frame blowup -- a real
efficiency regression at fixed action budget.

Confirms the triangulation's prediction and the adversarial lens: the
fix was proxy-polishing (coverage), not discovery-relevant. It should
NOT be wired to the submitted default. Stays opt-in/documented.

